From 93faaa1bbaf25d6c0719029318a82d69167bd366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chenhui Zhao <chenhui.zhao@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 18:32:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pubsub): Overhaul AF_XDP support with custom XDP program
 loading

Add support for loading a user-supplied XDP object file via the new
xdpProgPath connection property and CLI option, needed on platforms
without hardware flow steering for Ethernet frames (e.g. NXP i.MX943 ENETC).

Rewrite the XDP receive path to use per-packet callback processing with
proper 802.1Q VLAN parsing, and fix multiple bugs: UMEM fill queue
address calculation, TX ring rollover, negative errno handling in
xsk_socket__create, memory leaks on error paths, and fill queue
starvation from missing address recycling.

Add XDP multicast registration via ioctl(SIOCADDMULTI/SIOCDELMULTI),
packet hex dump debugging, startup option logging, and i.MX943 platform
documentation with a helper script.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Chenhui Zhao <chenhui.zhao@nxp.com>
