+pubsub_TSN_publisher & pubsub_TSN_loopback on NXP i.MX943 EVK
+===============================================================
+
+Overview
+--------
+
+This guide covers running the OPC UA PubSub TSN round-trip latency examples
+on two NXP i.MX943 EVK boards using the run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh script, which
+automates PTP synchronization, qdisc setup, and application launch with
+AF_XDP subscriber.
+
+  Board 1 (publisher, PTP slave) runs pubsub_TSN_publisher:
+    - Publishes an incrementing counter via raw Ethernet UADP (ethertype 0xB62C)
+    - Subscribes to the echoed counter from Board 2
+
+  Board 2 (loopback, PTP master) runs pubsub_TSN_loopback:
+    - Subscribes to the counter from Board 1
+    - Publishes (echoes) it back to Board 1
+
+Trace points for the round-trip:
+
+             +--------------+                  +----------------+
+          T1 | OPCUA PubSub |  T8           T5 | OPCUA loopback |  T4
+          |  |  Application |  ^            |  |  Application   |  ^
+          |  +--------------+  |            |  +----------------+  |
+          |  |    Board 1   |  |            |  |    Board 2     |  |
+          v  +--------------+  |            v  +----------------+  |
+          T2 |      TX      |  T7<--------- T6 |      RX       |  T3
+          |  +--------------+                  +----------------+  ^
+          |                                                        |
+          ----------------------------------------------------------
+
+
+Prerequisites
+-------------
+
+On both boards:
+
+  - NXP i.MX943 EVK with TSN-capable Ethernet on interface eth2
+  - Linux kernel with PREEMPT_RT and XDP support
+  - Boards connected directly via eth2 (peer-to-peer Ethernet cable)
+  - linuxptp installed (ptp4l, phc2sys)
+  - iproute2 installed (tc)
+  - ethtool installed
+  - Pre-built binaries available:
+      /root/open62541_example/pubsub_TSN_publisher    (on Board 1)
+      /root/open62541_example/pubsub_TSN_loopback     (on Board 2)
+  - XDP BPF program available:
+      /usr/lib/bpf/xdpfilt_alw_uadp.o                 (on both boards)
+  - PTP configuration file:
+      /etc/ptp4l_cfg/gPTP.cfg                         (on both boards)
+
+
+Running the Test
+----------------
+
+The script is located at /root/open62541_example/run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh
+on both boards. Always start the loopback (Board 2) before the publisher
+(Board 1).
+
+Board 2 (loopback, PTP master) - run first:
+
+  sudo /root/open62541_example/run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh
+
+Board 1 (publisher, PTP slave) - run after PTP has synchronized:
+
+  sudo /root/open62541_example/run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh -pub
+
+The script waits approximately 20 seconds for PTP synchronization and
+displays log output from ptp4l and phc2sys before launching the
+application. With DEBUG=true (default), counter values are printed to
+the console on both boards.
+
+To stop:
+  Press Ctrl+C. The script automatically cleans up on exit.
+
+
+What the Script Does
+--------------------
+
+The script automates the following steps in order:
+
+  1. Disables RX and TX VLAN hardware offload on the network interface
+     so the XDP program can inspect VLAN tags in packet headers.
+
+  2. Disables receive hashing to force all incoming traffic to RX queue 0.
+
+  3. Stops systemd-timesyncd and ntpd to prevent clock interference.
+
+  4. Configures a mqprio qdisc with 4 traffic classes (1 queue each,
+     hardware offload) for traffic class separation.
+
+  5. Starts ptp4l with gPTP configuration for PTP clock synchronization.
+     The loopback board runs as PTP master; the publisher board (invoked
+     with -pub) runs as PTP slave.
+
+  6. Starts phc2sys to synchronize the PTP hardware clock to
+     CLOCK_REALTIME (UTC offset 0).
+
+Script Configuration
+--------------------
+
+Edit the variables at the top of /root/open62541_example/run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh
+to match your environment:
+
+  NETIF="eth2"
+      Network interface for PubSub traffic.
+
+  XDP_PROG="/usr/lib/bpf/xdpfilt_alw_uadp.o"
+      Path to the XDP BPF program that filters UADP packets.
+
+  CYCLE_MS=100
+      Cycle time in milliseconds.
+
+  DEBUG=true
+      Set to true to enable console output (-enableconsolePrint).
+      Set to false for silent operation.
+
+  PUBLISHER_CMD="/root/open62541_example/pubsub_TSN_publisher"
+      Path to the publisher binary (used on Board 1 with -pub).
+
+  LOOPBACK_CMD="/root/open62541_example/pubsub_TSN_loopback"
+      Path to the loopback binary (used on Board 2, default mode).
+
+
+Cleanup
+-------
+
+On Ctrl+C or normal exit, the script automatically:
+  - Restores RX/TX VLAN offload and receive hashing on the interface
+  - Kills ptp4l and phc2sys
+  - Restarts systemd-timesyncd and ntpd
+
+To run cleanup manually without launching the application:
+
+  sudo /root/open62541_example/run_pubsub_TSN_xdp.sh -clean
